Through writing Python code in preload/content files, it is theoretically
possible to make CAT-SOOP pages do anything.  Beyond this, CAT-SOOP provides
methods to easily customize particular aspects of CAT-SOOP through implementing
custom question types, custom handlers, and plugins.  This page provides a
brief overview of each of these means of customization.

<tableofcontents/>

<catsoop-section>Custom Question Types</catsoop-section>

Course-local question types can add a new kind of interaction without changing
CAT-SOOP itself.

* [Designing Custom Question Types](CURRENT/qtypes) explains where question
  types live, how CAT-SOOP loads them, and the rendering and grading hooks a
  question type may implement.
* [Case Study: `self_partner`](CURRENT/self_partner) follows a stateful custom
  question type that lets students create and join their own groups.
* [Case Study: `sympy_check`](CURRENT/sympy_check) examines a symbolic-answer
  qtype whose CAT-SOOP adapter is separated from a reusable, independently
  tested checker library.

